---

# Key Learning

- SQL Injection can bypass authentication when user input is concatenated into SQL queries.
- SQL comments (`--`) can ignore the password verification.
- Authentication mechanisms should never trust raw user input.

---

# Mitigation

- Use parameterized queries (Prepared Statements).
- Validate and sanitize user input.
- Implement least-privilege database accounts.
- Avoid exposing SQL errors.
- Apply secure authentication and monitoring.

